      "questionText": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Complete the text, using the words given.</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dong Ho Village is a popular <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>12.1</label><input id='fbo-903927-0' class='ms fillblank-option-12' index='0' name='fbo-903927-0' type='text' size='20' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-903927-0' /></span></strong> in northern Vietnam, known for its traditional folk paintings. Visitors can<strong> </strong>take<strong> </strong>buses or motorbikes to explore this beautiful village, which is only a short distance from Hanoi. The village is a place where <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>12.2</label><input id='fbo-903927-1' class='ms fillblank-option-12' index='1' name='fbo-903927-1' type='text' size='20' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-903927-1' /></span></strong> can enjoy the art and learn about the culture of a craft village. Many tourists come to see the artists at work and buy paintings as souvenirs. Over the years, the village has made efforts to optimize the production process in order to <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>12.3</label><input id='fbo-903927-2' class='ms fillblank-option-12' index='2' name='fbo-903927-2' type='text' size='14' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-903927-2' /></span></strong> pollution and keep the environment clean, which helps maintain the charm of the area. The village has also worked to preserve their <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>12.4</label><input id='fbo-903927-3' class='ms fillblank-option-12' index='3' name='fbo-903927-3' type='text' size='23' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-903927-3' /></span></strong> of making paintings but still <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>12.5</label><input id='fbo-903927-4' class='ms fillblank-option-12' index='4' name='fbo-903927-4' type='text' size='8' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-903927-4' /></span></strong> the time, so customers do not have to wait long to receive high-quality paintings.&nbsp;By doing this, artisans can meet the growing demand from tourists while keeping their traditions alive. It is a great example of how a local community can both preserve and share its culture.</p>",
